\fIExpand\fR
.IX Subsection "Expand"
.PP
.Vb 1
\& Expand LABEL CLASS PARAM...
.Ve
.PP
Declares a named term expander which can be used to expand index queries
using either the explicit pipeline notation (\f(CW\*(C`|LABEL|...\*(C'\fR), or implicit
expansion heuristics on a per-index basis.  Conceptually,
each expander in a pipeline operates on the set of terms returned by the
previous expander in the pipeline, and the set returned by the final expander
in the pipeline represents that set of index values which qualify as \*(L"matches\*(R" to the term queried.
.PP
\&\fI\s-1LABEL\s0\fR is a label string
used to identify the expander in user-specified pipelines.
If \fI\s-1LABEL\s0\fR is also the \fI\s-1LONGNAME\s0\fR of an index field declared in Indices,
then the corresponding expander is used implicitly if no explicit pipeline is
specified or if the default pipeline \f(CW\*(C`|\-\*(C'\fR is used.
.PP
\&\fI\s-1CLASS\s0\fR is a string representing the expansion function to use, and
\&\fI\s-1PARAM\s0...\fR are additional parameters to the expansion function.
Currently supported expander classes are:
.IP "Id" 4
.IX Item "Id"
.Vb 2
\& Expand LABEL Id
\& Expand LABEL Null
.Ve
.Sp
Identity expander (no-op).  Parameters: none.
.IP "Case" 4
.IX Item "Case"
.Vb 1
\&  Expand LABEL Case LANG
.Ve
.Sp
Letter-case expander (upper\- vs. lower-case).
Parameters: \f(CW\*(C`LANG\*(C'\fR, a language string as accepted by the
\&\s-1LANG\s0 declaration.  In particular, the
\&\*(L"language\*(R" \f(CW\*(C`Generic\*(C'\fR can be used to specify that
the C99 locale settings should be used to provide
upper/lower\-case mappings on wide character strings:
in this case, you must ensure that the \fI\s-1LC_CTYPE\s0\fR
enviornment variable for the \s-1DDC\s0 process is set
appropriately for the corpus and runtime query data.
.Sp
Note that not all letter-case variants are created
by this expander (\*(L"McTaggart problem\*(R").
.IP "ToLower" 4
.IX Item "ToLower"
.Vb 1
\&  Expand LABEL ToLower LANG
.Ve
.Sp
Forces all terms to lower-case.
Parameters: \f(CW\*(C`LANG\*(C'\fR, a language string as accepted by the
\&\s-1LANG\s0 declaration, or \f(CW\*(C`Generic\*(C'\fR to use the C99 locale settings.
.IP "ToUpper" 4
.IX Item "ToUpper"
.Vb 1
\&  Expand LABEL ToUpper LANG
.Ve
.Sp
Forces all terms to upper-case.
Parameters: \f(CW\*(C`LANG\*(C'\fR, a language string as accepted by the
\&\s-1LANG\s0 declaration, or \f(CW\*(C`Generic\*(C'\fR to use the C99 locale settings.
.IP "Infl" 4
.IX Item "Infl"
.Vb 2
\& Expand LABEL Infl LANG
\& Expand LABEL Morph LANG
.Ve
.Sp
Inflectional variant expander using built-in morphology
tables.  Parameters: \f(CW\*(C`LANG\*(C'\fR, a language string as
accepted by the \s-1LANG\s0 declaration.
.IP "Cab" 4
.IX Item "Cab"
.Vb 1
\& Expand LABEL Cab URL TIMEOUT DEBUG
.Ve
.Sp
Orthographic variant expander which queries an external \s-1DTA::CAB\s0 \s-1HTTP\s0 server.
Parameters:
.RS 4
.IP "\s-1URL\s0" 4
.IX Item "URL"
\&\s-1URL\s0 of the \s-1DTA::CAB\s0 \s-1HTTP\s0 server to be queried with \s-1GET\s0 request.
The underlying implementation appends a URL-encoded parameter \f(CW\*(C`qd=DATA\*(C'\fR
to this \s-1URL\s0 before requesting data from the server, where \fI\s-1DATA\s0\fR is
a newline-separated list of types to be expanded.
The data format returned by the server is assumed to be a list
of expanded types separated by TABs, newlines, and/or carriage returns.
Empty types in the output are ignored.
.IP "\s-1TIMEOUT\s0" 4
.IX Item "TIMEOUT"
Timeout in seconds for the expansion query.
If the timeout is exceeded, a warning is printed and the
\&\s-1CAB\s0 expander behaves like an Id expander, returning
the same set it was passed.
.IP "\s-1DEBUG\s0" 4
.IX Item "DEBUG"
Boolean flag for debugging.  If set to a true value, all data
passed to and from the external \s-1DTA::CAB\s0 server will be echoed
to stderr.  Not for production use.
.RE
.RS 4
.RE
.IP "Chain" 4
.IX Item "Chain"
.Vb 1
\& Expand LABEL Chain PIPELINE...
.Ve
.Sp
Assigns a label to a chain of previously defined expanders.
Takes a \f(CW\*(C`PIPELINE\*(C'\fR of expander labels as its argument:
expander labels in \f(CW\*(C`PIPELINE\*(C'\fR may separated by whitespace
and/or the \f(CW\*(C`|\*(C'\fR symbol (multiple consecutive delimiters are ignored).
Note that an empty expander chain is equivalent to an Id expander.
.PP
\&\s-1DDC\s0 ensures that the following expander labels are defined,
instantiating them with default parameters only if no other
expander with the same label is explicitly defined in the opt-file:
.IP "id" 4
.IX Item "id"
Defined as \f(CW\*(C`Expand id Id\*(C'\fR
.IP "null" 4
.IX Item "null"
Defined as \f(CW\*(C`Expand null Id\*(C'\fR
.IP "case" 4
.IX Item "case"
Defined as \f(CW\*(C`Expand case LANG\*(C'\fR unless the Utf8 flag was set,
in which case the default \fIcase\fR expander is defined as \f(CW\*(C`Expand case Generic\*(C'\fR.
.IP "infl" 4
.IX Item "infl"
Defined as \f(CW\*(C`Expand infl LANG\*(C'\fR.
.IP "Token" 4
.IX Item "Token"
Default expansion chain for the \fIToken\fR index.
Usually defined as \f(CW\*(C`Expand Token Chain infl case\*(C'\fR,
but note that the \f(CW\*(C`case\*(C'\fR component will be omitted from
the default chain unless the legacy CaseInsensitive flag is set,
and the \f(CW\*(C`infl\*(C'\fR component will be omitted if
the legacy DisableDefaultQueryLexicalExpansion
option is set.
